{"version":1,"generated":"2026-04-10T04:49:39Z","windows":[{"key":"AppGalleryWindow","text":"## AppGalleryWindow\n\nThe **App Gallery** is the built-in app launcher and dock-pinning interface.\nIt is always pinned as the leftmost icon in the dock and cannot be removed.\n\n---\n\n### Layout Overview\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  App Gallery                                 [?] [−] [×]        │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  ┌──────┐ ┌──────┐ ┌──────┐ ┌──────┐ ┌──────┐                 │\n│  │ Icon │ │ Icon │ │ Icon │ │ Icon │ │ Icon │  (scrollable)    │\n│  │ Name │ │ Name │ │ Name │ │ Name │ │ Name │                  │\n│  └──────┘ └──────┘ └──────┘ └──────┘ └──────┘                 │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Opening Apps\n\n- **Single click** an app tile to open it (or restore its window if already open)\n\n---\n\n### Pinning to the Dock\n\n1. **Click-and-hold** an app tile until the drag starts\n2. A ghost icon with a **+ Pin to Dock** label follows the cursor\n3. Drag to the **dock bar** at the bottom of the screen\n4. An animated spacer shows where the icon will land\n5. Release to pin the app permanently\n\n---\n\n### Adding a Desktop Shortcut\n\n1. **Click-and-hold** an app tile\n2. Drag to the **desktop background** area (not the dock)\n3. The ghost label changes to **+ Add to Desktop**\n4. Release to create a shortcut icon on the desktop\n\n---\n\n### Icon Loading\n\nApp icons are loaded asynchronously from GitHub.  A placeholder is shown\nuntil the real icon downloads. Icons are cached for the session.\n\n---","screenshot":""},{"key":"ChatWindow","text":"## ChatWindow\n\nThe **Chat Window** is a multi-provider AI conversation interface supporting\nGemini, OpenAI (GPT), and Anthropic (Claude) models.\n\n---\n\n### Layout Overview\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  [Model Dropdown ▼]   [Copy Chat]            [?] [−] [×]        │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                                  │\n│    User:  Hello, tell me about NCalc.          ──────────────▶  │\n│                                                                  │\n│    AI:    NCalc is a pure-C# expression...  ◀────────────────   │\n│                    [▼ expand]                                    │\n│                                                                  │\n│    ● ● ●   (typing indicator)                                    │\n│                                                                  │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  [↕]  Type a message here...                   [➤ Send]         │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Model Selection\n\nUse the **Model Dropdown** in the title bar to choose the AI provider and model:\n\n- **Gemini 2.5 Flash** — Google's fast multimodal model\n- **GPT-4o** — OpenAI flagship model\n- **Claude 3.5 Sonnet** — Anthropic's balanced model\n- Additional models appear as they become available\n\nAll requests are routed through a Cloudflare Worker proxy — no API keys\nare stored in the browser.\n\n---\n\n### Sending Messages\n\n- Type your message in the input box at the bottom\n- Press **Enter** to send, or click **➤**\n- Press **Shift+Enter** to insert a newline without sending\n- Click **↕** to expand the input area for longer messages\n\n---\n\n### Message Bubbles\n\n- **User messages** appear on the right\n- **AI messages** appear on the left with a provider avatar\n- Long AI messages (> 5 lines) are collapsed; click **▼ expand** to read the full reply\n- A **● ● ●** animation indicates the AI is processing your request\n\n---\n\n### Copy Chat\n\nClick **Copy Chat** in the title bar to copy the full conversation to the\nclipboard as formatted markdown, including model labels.\n\n---\n\n### Error Handling\n\nIf the API returns a billing or quota error, a banner appears at the top\nof the chat. It auto-dismisses after 20 seconds, or click **×** to close it.\n\n---","screenshot":""},{"key":"GalleryWindow","text":"## GalleryWindow\n\nThe **Gallery Window** is an image browser for setting desktop wallpapers.\n\n---\n\n### Layout Overview\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  Gallery                                     [?] [−] [×]        │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  ┌───┐ ┌───┐ ┌───┐ ┌───┐ ┌───┐ ┌───┐ ┌───┐                    │\n│  │img│ │img│ │img│ │img│ │img│ │img│ │img│   (scrollable grid) │\n│  └───┘ └───┘ └───┘ └───┘ └───┘ └───┘ └───┘                    │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Setting a Wallpaper\n\n**Method 1 — Drag and drop:**\n1. Click and hold an image thumbnail\n2. A ghost icon follows your cursor with a **+** badge\n3. Drag to the desktop background area\n4. Release to set as wallpaper\n\n**Method 2 — Right-click:**\n1. Right-click an image thumbnail\n2. Choose **Set as Wallpaper**\n\n---\n\n### Image Thumbnails\n\n- Thumbnails load asynchronously from the background manifest\n- Hover over a thumbnail to see the image **name** and **resolution** in a tooltip\n- Images are sourced from `StreamingAssets/Backgrounds/`\n\n---\n\n### Right-Click Menu\n\n- **Set as Wallpaper** — apply this image as the desktop background\n- **Close Gallery** — close the window\n\n---","screenshot":""},{"key":"DebugLogWindow","text":"## DebugLogWindow\n\nThe **Debug Log Window** captures Unity's `Debug.Log`, warnings, and errors\nin real-time with colour coding and text-selection support.\n\n---\n\n### Layout Overview\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  [Clear]  [Copy]  [⇄ Wrap]                  [?] [−] [×]         │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  [13:42:01] SceneManager loaded                                  │\n│  [13:42:02] XmlWindow: loaded 142 nodes                          │\n│  [13:42:05] ERROR: NullReferenceException in ...    ← red        │\n│                                                                  │\n│  (auto-scrolls to newest; select text with mouse)                │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Title Bar Buttons\n\n- **Clear** — remove all captured log entries\n- **Copy** — copy the full log to the clipboard as plain text\n- **⇄ Wrap** — toggle word wrap (wrapped = vertical scroll only; unwrapped = horizontal + vertical)\n\n---\n\n### Log Colours\n\n- **White** — standard `Debug.Log` messages\n- **Red** — `Debug.LogError` and unhandled exceptions\n\n---\n\n### Features\n\n- Subscribes to `Application.logMessageReceived` — captures logs from all sources\n- Auto-scrolls to the bottom as new messages arrive\n- While drag-selecting text near the viewport edges, the scroll view accelerates to let you select long entries\n- When the window is in the background (not focused), the title indicator turns **green** when new logs arrive; resets when you bring the window to front\n\n---","screenshot":""},{"key":"NotesWindow","text":"## NotesWindow\n\nThe **Notes Window** is a markdown editor with GitHub sync, undo/redo,\nand a rich-text preview mode.\n\n---\n\n### Layout Overview\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  [Edit]  [⇄ Wrap]                           [?] [−] [×]         │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                                  │\n│   Rich-text display (view mode)                                  │\n│   or raw markdown editor (edit mode)                             │\n│                                                                  │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### View / Edit Modes\n\n- **View mode** (default) — renders markdown as styled rich text\n- Click **Edit** to switch to the raw markdown editor\n- Click **Done** (or press `Ctrl+S`) to save and return to view mode\n\n---\n\n### Markdown Support\n\n| Syntax | Renders As |\n|---|---|\n| `# Heading` | Large bold heading |\n| `## Subheading` | Medium bold heading |\n| `**bold**` | Bold text |\n| `*italic*` | Italic text |\n| `- item` | Bullet point (•) |\n| `---` | Horizontal rule |\n\n---\n\n### Text Wrap\n\nClick the **⇄** button to toggle word wrap.\n\n- **On** (default) — text wraps within the window; vertical scroll only\n- **Off** — long lines scroll horizontally; useful for tables or code blocks\n\n---\n\n### Keyboard Shortcuts\n\n- `Ctrl+S` — save (while editing)\n- `Escape` — cancel edit without saving\n\n---\n\n### GitHub Sync\n\nNotes are automatically loaded from GitHub on open and saved on Done.\nIf GitHub is unavailable a yellow warning banner appears with a **Retry** button.\nThe note is also kept in StreamingAssets as a local fallback.\n\n---","screenshot":""},{"key":"NotesWindow","text":"## NotesWindow\n\nThe **Notes Window** is a markdown editor with GitHub sync, undo/redo,\nand a rich-text preview mode.\n\n---\n\n### Layout Overview\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  [Edit]  [⇄ Wrap]                           [?] [−] [×]         │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                                  │\n│   Rich-text display (view mode)                                  │\n│   or raw markdown editor (edit mode)                             │\n│                                                                  │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### View / Edit Modes\n\n- **View mode** (default) — renders markdown as styled rich text\n- Click **Edit** to switch to the raw markdown editor\n- Click **Done** (or press `Ctrl+S`) to save and return to view mode\n\n---\n\n### Markdown Support\n\n| Syntax | Renders As |\n|---|---|\n| `# Heading` | Large bold heading |\n| `## Subheading` | Medium bold heading |\n| `**bold**` | Bold text |\n| `*italic*` | Italic text |\n| `- item` | Bullet point (•) |\n| `---` | Horizontal rule |\n\n---\n\n### Text Wrap\n\nClick the **⇄** button to toggle word wrap.\n\n- **On** (default) — text wraps within the window; vertical scroll only\n- **Off** — long lines scroll horizontally; useful for tables or code blocks\n\n---\n\n### Keyboard Shortcuts\n\n- `Ctrl+S` — save (while editing)\n- `Escape` — cancel edit without saving\n\n---\n\n### GitHub Sync\n\nNotes are automatically loaded from GitHub on open and saved on Done.\nIf GitHub is unavailable a yellow warning banner appears with a **Retry** button.\nThe note is also kept in StreamingAssets as a local fallback.\n\n---","screenshot":""},{"key":"NotesWindow","text":"## NotesWindow\n\nThe **Notes Window** is a markdown editor with GitHub sync, undo/redo,\nand a rich-text preview mode.\n\n---\n\n### Layout Overview\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  [Edit]  [⇄ Wrap]                           [?] [−] [×]         │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                                  │\n│   Rich-text display (view mode)                                  │\n│   or raw markdown editor (edit mode)                             │\n│                                                                  │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### View / Edit Modes\n\n- **View mode** (default) — renders markdown as styled rich text\n- Click **Edit** to switch to the raw markdown editor\n- Click **Done** (or press `Ctrl+S`) to save and return to view mode\n\n---\n\n### Markdown Support\n\n| Syntax | Renders As |\n|---|---|\n| `# Heading` | Large bold heading |\n| `## Subheading` | Medium bold heading |\n| `**bold**` | Bold text |\n| `*italic*` | Italic text |\n| `- item` | Bullet point (•) |\n| `---` | Horizontal rule |\n\n---\n\n### Text Wrap\n\nClick the **⇄** button to toggle word wrap.\n\n- **On** (default) — text wraps within the window; vertical scroll only\n- **Off** — long lines scroll horizontally; useful for tables or code blocks\n\n---\n\n### Keyboard Shortcuts\n\n- `Ctrl+S` — save (while editing)\n- `Escape` — cancel edit without saving\n\n---\n\n### GitHub Sync\n\nNotes are automatically loaded from GitHub on open and saved on Done.\nIf GitHub is unavailable a yellow warning banner appears with a **Retry** button.\nThe note is also kept in StreamingAssets as a local fallback.\n\n---","screenshot":""},{"key":"XmlWindow","text":"## XmlWindow\n\nThe **XML Window** is a hierarchical XML tree editor with in-place editing,\ndrag-to-reorder, search filtering, and GitHub sync.\n\n---\n\n### Layout Overview\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  [Search ⌕]  [</> Validate]  [⚙ Options]     [?] [−] [×]       │\n├──┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  │ ▼ root                                                        │\n│  │   ▼ element  attr=\"value\"                                     │\n│Line│       leaf content                                          │\n│Nos│   ▶ collapsed                                                │\n│   │                                                              │\n└──┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Title Bar Buttons\n\n- **⌕** — Toggle the search/filter bar (`Ctrl+F` / `Cmd+F`)\n- **</>** — Run XML well-formedness validation\n- **⚙** — Options menu (text wrapping, line numbers)\n\n---\n\n### Tree View\n\n- **▶ / ▼** — expand or collapse a node\n- **Click** a node to select it\n- **Double-click** a tag name, attribute value, or leaf content to edit it in-place\n  - `Tab` or `Enter` to commit\n  - `Escape` to cancel\n- **Right-click** a node for the context menu (add child, delete, etc.)\n- **Line number gutter** (left side) — shows sequential line numbers with selection highlight\n\n---\n\n### Drag-to-Reorder\n\n- **Drag** any node to reorder within its parent\n- Drop indicators show **before**, **after**, or **as child** insertion positions\n- Dragging between XML fragments is supported\n\n---\n\n### Search / Filter\n\nPress `Ctrl+F` or click the search button to open the filter bar.\n\n- Filters the tree in real-time as you type\n- Matches **tag names**, **attribute keys**, **attribute values**, and **leaf content**\n- Only matching nodes and their ancestors are shown\n- Press `Escape` or click the search button again to clear\n\n---\n\n### Options Menu\n\n- **Wrap Text** — toggle word wrap (affects horizontal scroll behaviour)\n- **Show Line Numbers** — show or hide the line-number gutter\n\n---\n\n### Keyboard Shortcuts\n\n- `Ctrl+F` — open/close search\n- `Tab` / `Enter` — commit in-place edit\n- `Escape` — cancel edit or close search\n\n---","screenshot":""},{"key":"XmlWindow","text":"## XmlWindow\n\nThe **XML Window** is a hierarchical XML tree editor with in-place editing,\ndrag-to-reorder, search filtering, and GitHub sync.\n\n---\n\n### Layout Overview\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  [Search ⌕]  [</> Validate]  [⚙ Options]     [?] [−] [×]       │\n├──┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  │ ▼ root                                                        │\n│  │   ▼ element  attr=\"value\"                                     │\n│Line│       leaf content                                          │\n│Nos│   ▶ collapsed                                                │\n│   │                                                              │\n└──┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Title Bar Buttons\n\n- **⌕** — Toggle the search/filter bar (`Ctrl+F` / `Cmd+F`)\n- **</>** — Run XML well-formedness validation\n- **⚙** — Options menu (text wrapping, line numbers)\n\n---\n\n### Tree View\n\n- **▶ / ▼** — expand or collapse a node\n- **Click** a node to select it\n- **Double-click** a tag name, attribute value, or leaf content to edit it in-place\n  - `Tab` or `Enter` to commit\n  - `Escape` to cancel\n- **Right-click** a node for the context menu (add child, delete, etc.)\n- **Line number gutter** (left side) — shows sequential line numbers with selection highlight\n\n---\n\n### Drag-to-Reorder\n\n- **Drag** any node to reorder within its parent\n- Drop indicators show **before**, **after**, or **as child** insertion positions\n- Dragging between XML fragments is supported\n\n---\n\n### Search / Filter\n\nPress `Ctrl+F` or click the search button to open the filter bar.\n\n- Filters the tree in real-time as you type\n- Matches **tag names**, **attribute keys**, **attribute values**, and **leaf content**\n- Only matching nodes and their ancestors are shown\n- Press `Escape` or click the search button again to clear\n\n---\n\n### Options Menu\n\n- **Wrap Text** — toggle word wrap (affects horizontal scroll behaviour)\n- **Show Line Numbers** — show or hide the line-number gutter\n\n---\n\n### Keyboard Shortcuts\n\n- `Ctrl+F` — open/close search\n- `Tab` / `Enter` — commit in-place edit\n- `Escape` — cancel edit or close search\n\n---","screenshot":""},{"key":"UmlWindow","text":"## UmlWindow\n\nThe **UML Window** is an interactive UML class diagram editor supporting\nsix relationship types, auto-layout, and SAI/Gorp XML import.\n\n---\n\n### Layout Overview\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  [Auto-layout]  [Import]  [Save]            [?] [−] [×]         │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                                  │\n│    ┌───────────────┐          ┌─────────────────┐               │\n│    │  ClassName    │ ──────▷  │  AnotherClass   │               │\n│    │───────────────│          │─────────────────│               │\n│    │ + field: Type │          │ + method(): void│               │\n│    │───────────────│          └─────────────────┘               │\n│    │ + method()    │                                             │\n│    └───────────────┘                                             │\n│                                                                  │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Class Boxes\n\nEach class box has three sections: **name**, **attributes**, and **methods**.\n\n- **Click** to select a class\n- **Drag** to move the class box on the canvas\n- **Double-click** the class name to rename it\n- **Right-click** for the context menu:\n  - Add attribute / Add method\n  - Delete class\n  - Connect From Here (start a relationship)\n\n---\n\n### Members (Attributes & Methods)\n\n- **Double-click** a member to rename it in-place\n- **Drag** members to reorder within the class or move to another class\n- **Right-click** a member for options (delete, change visibility)\n- Visibility icons: `+` public, `-` private, `#` protected, `~` package\n\n---\n\n### Relationships\n\nSix relationship types are supported:\n\n| Symbol | Type | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| ──────▷ | Association | General use/reference |\n| ───────▷ | Dependency | Temporary dependency |\n| ──────▻ | Realization | Implements interface |\n| ──────▷ | Inheritance | Extends class |\n| ◇──────  | Aggregation | Has-a (weak) |\n| ◆──────  | Composition | Has-a (strong, owned) |\n\n- **Connect From Here** — right-click a class, choose *Connect From Here*, then click the target class\n- Hover over a relationship line to see its type label; after 2.5 s a tooltip shows the full description\n- Parallel connections between the same two classes are automatically separated by 25 px\n- Multiplicity labels appear along relationship lines (e.g. `1`, `0..*`)\n\n---\n\n### Canvas\n\n- **Left-drag** empty canvas to pan\n- **Right-click** canvas for: Add Class, Auto-Layout, Import, Save\n- **Auto-Layout** — arranges all classes automatically to avoid overlaps\n\n---\n\n### File Operations\n\n- **Save** — serialises the diagram to XML and saves to GitHub\n- **Import** — loads from a SAI XML, Gorp XML, or custom UML XML file\n- Files are loaded from GitHub or StreamingAssets fallback on open\n\n---","screenshot":""},{"key":"UmlWindow","text":"## UmlWindow\n\nThe **UML Window** is an interactive UML class diagram editor supporting\nsix relationship types, auto-layout, and SAI/Gorp XML import.\n\n---\n\n### Layout Overview\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  [Auto-layout]  [Import]  [Save]            [?] [−] [×]         │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                                  │\n│    ┌───────────────┐          ┌─────────────────┐               │\n│    │  ClassName    │ ──────▷  │  AnotherClass   │               │\n│    │───────────────│          │─────────────────│               │\n│    │ + field: Type │          │ + method(): void│               │\n│    │───────────────│          └─────────────────┘               │\n│    │ + method()    │                                             │\n│    └───────────────┘                                             │\n│                                                                  │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Class Boxes\n\nEach class box has three sections: **name**, **attributes**, and **methods**.\n\n- **Click** to select a class\n- **Drag** to move the class box on the canvas\n- **Double-click** the class name to rename it\n- **Right-click** for the context menu:\n  - Add attribute / Add method\n  - Delete class\n  - Connect From Here (start a relationship)\n\n---\n\n### Members (Attributes & Methods)\n\n- **Double-click** a member to rename it in-place\n- **Drag** members to reorder within the class or move to another class\n- **Right-click** a member for options (delete, change visibility)\n- Visibility icons: `+` public, `-` private, `#` protected, `~` package\n\n---\n\n### Relationships\n\nSix relationship types are supported:\n\n| Symbol | Type | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| ──────▷ | Association | General use/reference |\n| ───────▷ | Dependency | Temporary dependency |\n| ──────▻ | Realization | Implements interface |\n| ──────▷ | Inheritance | Extends class |\n| ◇──────  | Aggregation | Has-a (weak) |\n| ◆──────  | Composition | Has-a (strong, owned) |\n\n- **Connect From Here** — right-click a class, choose *Connect From Here*, then click the target class\n- Hover over a relationship line to see its type label; after 2.5 s a tooltip shows the full description\n- Parallel connections between the same two classes are automatically separated by 25 px\n- Multiplicity labels appear along relationship lines (e.g. `1`, `0..*`)\n\n---\n\n### Canvas\n\n- **Left-drag** empty canvas to pan\n- **Right-click** canvas for: Add Class, Auto-Layout, Import, Save\n- **Auto-Layout** — arranges all classes automatically to avoid overlaps\n\n---\n\n### File Operations\n\n- **Save** — serialises the diagram to XML and saves to GitHub\n- **Import** — loads from a SAI XML, Gorp XML, or custom UML XML file\n- Files are loaded from GitHub or StreamingAssets fallback on open\n\n---","screenshot":""},{"key":"UmlWindow","text":"## UmlWindow\n\nThe **UML Window** is an interactive UML class diagram editor supporting\nsix relationship types, auto-layout, and SAI/Gorp XML import.\n\n---\n\n### Layout Overview\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  [Auto-layout]  [Import]  [Save]            [?] [−] [×]         │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                                  │\n│    ┌───────────────┐          ┌─────────────────┐               │\n│    │  ClassName    │ ──────▷  │  AnotherClass   │               │\n│    │───────────────│          │─────────────────│               │\n│    │ + field: Type │          │ + method(): void│               │\n│    │───────────────│          └─────────────────┘               │\n│    │ + method()    │                                             │\n│    └───────────────┘                                             │\n│                                                                  │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Class Boxes\n\nEach class box has three sections: **name**, **attributes**, and **methods**.\n\n- **Click** to select a class\n- **Drag** to move the class box on the canvas\n- **Double-click** the class name to rename it\n- **Right-click** for the context menu:\n  - Add attribute / Add method\n  - Delete class\n  - Connect From Here (start a relationship)\n\n---\n\n### Members (Attributes & Methods)\n\n- **Double-click** a member to rename it in-place\n- **Drag** members to reorder within the class or move to another class\n- **Right-click** a member for options (delete, change visibility)\n- Visibility icons: `+` public, `-` private, `#` protected, `~` package\n\n---\n\n### Relationships\n\nSix relationship types are supported:\n\n| Symbol | Type | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| ──────▷ | Association | General use/reference |\n| ───────▷ | Dependency | Temporary dependency |\n| ──────▻ | Realization | Implements interface |\n| ──────▷ | Inheritance | Extends class |\n| ◇──────  | Aggregation | Has-a (weak) |\n| ◆──────  | Composition | Has-a (strong, owned) |\n\n- **Connect From Here** — right-click a class, choose *Connect From Here*, then click the target class\n- Hover over a relationship line to see its type label; after 2.5 s a tooltip shows the full description\n- Parallel connections between the same two classes are automatically separated by 25 px\n- Multiplicity labels appear along relationship lines (e.g. `1`, `0..*`)\n\n---\n\n### Canvas\n\n- **Left-drag** empty canvas to pan\n- **Right-click** canvas for: Add Class, Auto-Layout, Import, Save\n- **Auto-Layout** — arranges all classes automatically to avoid overlaps\n\n---\n\n### File Operations\n\n- **Save** — serialises the diagram to XML and saves to GitHub\n- **Import** — loads from a SAI XML, Gorp XML, or custom UML XML file\n- Files are loaded from GitHub or StreamingAssets fallback on open\n\n---","screenshot":""},{"key":"XmlWindow","text":"## XmlWindow\n\nThe **XML Window** is a hierarchical XML tree editor with in-place editing,\ndrag-to-reorder, search filtering, and GitHub sync.\n\n---\n\n### Layout Overview\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  [Search ⌕]  [</> Validate]  [⚙ Options]     [?] [−] [×]       │\n├──┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  │ ▼ root                                                        │\n│  │   ▼ element  attr=\"value\"                                     │\n│Line│       leaf content                                          │\n│Nos│   ▶ collapsed                                                │\n│   │                                                              │\n└──┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Title Bar Buttons\n\n- **⌕** — Toggle the search/filter bar (`Ctrl+F` / `Cmd+F`)\n- **</>** — Run XML well-formedness validation\n- **⚙** — Options menu (text wrapping, line numbers)\n\n---\n\n### Tree View\n\n- **▶ / ▼** — expand or collapse a node\n- **Click** a node to select it\n- **Double-click** a tag name, attribute value, or leaf content to edit it in-place\n  - `Tab` or `Enter` to commit\n  - `Escape` to cancel\n- **Right-click** a node for the context menu (add child, delete, etc.)\n- **Line number gutter** (left side) — shows sequential line numbers with selection highlight\n\n---\n\n### Drag-to-Reorder\n\n- **Drag** any node to reorder within its parent\n- Drop indicators show **before**, **after**, or **as child** insertion positions\n- Dragging between XML fragments is supported\n\n---\n\n### Search / Filter\n\nPress `Ctrl+F` or click the search button to open the filter bar.\n\n- Filters the tree in real-time as you type\n- Matches **tag names**, **attribute keys**, **attribute values**, and **leaf content**\n- Only matching nodes and their ancestors are shown\n- Press `Escape` or click the search button again to clear\n\n---\n\n### Options Menu\n\n- **Wrap Text** — toggle word wrap (affects horizontal scroll behaviour)\n- **Show Line Numbers** — show or hide the line-number gutter\n\n---\n\n### Keyboard Shortcuts\n\n- `Ctrl+F` — open/close search\n- `Tab` / `Enter` — commit in-place edit\n- `Escape` — cancel edit or close search\n\n---","screenshot":""},{"key":"XmlWindow","text":"## XmlWindow\n\nThe **XML Window** is a hierarchical XML tree editor with in-place editing,\ndrag-to-reorder, search filtering, and GitHub sync.\n\n---\n\n### Layout Overview\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  [Search ⌕]  [</> Validate]  [⚙ Options]     [?] [−] [×]       │\n├──┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  │ ▼ root                                                        │\n│  │   ▼ element  attr=\"value\"                                     │\n│Line│       leaf content                                          │\n│Nos│   ▶ collapsed                                                │\n│   │                                                              │\n└──┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Title Bar Buttons\n\n- **⌕** — Toggle the search/filter bar (`Ctrl+F` / `Cmd+F`)\n- **</>** — Run XML well-formedness validation\n- **⚙** — Options menu (text wrapping, line numbers)\n\n---\n\n### Tree View\n\n- **▶ / ▼** — expand or collapse a node\n- **Click** a node to select it\n- **Double-click** a tag name, attribute value, or leaf content to edit it in-place\n  - `Tab` or `Enter` to commit\n  - `Escape` to cancel\n- **Right-click** a node for the context menu (add child, delete, etc.)\n- **Line number gutter** (left side) — shows sequential line numbers with selection highlight\n\n---\n\n### Drag-to-Reorder\n\n- **Drag** any node to reorder within its parent\n- Drop indicators show **before**, **after**, or **as child** insertion positions\n- Dragging between XML fragments is supported\n\n---\n\n### Search / Filter\n\nPress `Ctrl+F` or click the search button to open the filter bar.\n\n- Filters the tree in real-time as you type\n- Matches **tag names**, **attribute keys**, **attribute values**, and **leaf content**\n- Only matching nodes and their ancestors are shown\n- Press `Escape` or click the search button again to clear\n\n---\n\n### Options Menu\n\n- **Wrap Text** — toggle word wrap (affects horizontal scroll behaviour)\n- **Show Line Numbers** — show or hide the line-number gutter\n\n---\n\n### Keyboard Shortcuts\n\n- `Ctrl+F` — open/close search\n- `Tab` / `Enter` — commit in-place edit\n- `Escape` — cancel edit or close search\n\n---","screenshot":""},{"key":"XmlWindow","text":"## XmlWindow\n\nThe **XML Window** is a hierarchical XML tree editor with in-place editing,\ndrag-to-reorder, search filtering, and GitHub sync.\n\n---\n\n### Layout Overview\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  [Search ⌕]  [</> Validate]  [⚙ Options]     [?] [−] [×]       │\n├──┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  │ ▼ root                                                        │\n│  │   ▼ element  attr=\"value\"                                     │\n│Line│       leaf content                                          │\n│Nos│   ▶ collapsed                                                │\n│   │                                                              │\n└──┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Title Bar Buttons\n\n- **⌕** — Toggle the search/filter bar (`Ctrl+F` / `Cmd+F`)\n- **</>** — Run XML well-formedness validation\n- **⚙** — Options menu (text wrapping, line numbers)\n\n---\n\n### Tree View\n\n- **▶ / ▼** — expand or collapse a node\n- **Click** a node to select it\n- **Double-click** a tag name, attribute value, or leaf content to edit it in-place\n  - `Tab` or `Enter` to commit\n  - `Escape` to cancel\n- **Right-click** a node for the context menu (add child, delete, etc.)\n- **Line number gutter** (left side) — shows sequential line numbers with selection highlight\n\n---\n\n### Drag-to-Reorder\n\n- **Drag** any node to reorder within its parent\n- Drop indicators show **before**, **after**, or **as child** insertion positions\n- Dragging between XML fragments is supported\n\n---\n\n### Search / Filter\n\nPress `Ctrl+F` or click the search button to open the filter bar.\n\n- Filters the tree in real-time as you type\n- Matches **tag names**, **attribute keys**, **attribute values**, and **leaf content**\n- Only matching nodes and their ancestors are shown\n- Press `Escape` or click the search button again to clear\n\n---\n\n### Options Menu\n\n- **Wrap Text** — toggle word wrap (affects horizontal scroll behaviour)\n- **Show Line Numbers** — show or hide the line-number gutter\n\n---\n\n### Keyboard Shortcuts\n\n- `Ctrl+F` — open/close search\n- `Tab` / `Enter` — commit in-place edit\n- `Escape` — cancel edit or close search\n\n---","screenshot":""},{"key":"XmlWindow","text":"## XmlWindow\n\nThe **XML Window** is a hierarchical XML tree editor with in-place editing,\ndrag-to-reorder, search filtering, and GitHub sync.\n\n---\n\n### Layout Overview\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  [Search ⌕]  [</> Validate]  [⚙ Options]     [?] [−] [×]       │\n├──┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  │ ▼ root                                                        │\n│  │   ▼ element  attr=\"value\"                                     │\n│Line│       leaf content                                          │\n│Nos│   ▶ collapsed                                                │\n│   │                                                              │\n└──┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Title Bar Buttons\n\n- **⌕** — Toggle the search/filter bar (`Ctrl+F` / `Cmd+F`)\n- **</>** — Run XML well-formedness validation\n- **⚙** — Options menu (text wrapping, line numbers)\n\n---\n\n### Tree View\n\n- **▶ / ▼** — expand or collapse a node\n- **Click** a node to select it\n- **Double-click** a tag name, attribute value, or leaf content to edit it in-place\n  - `Tab` or `Enter` to commit\n  - `Escape` to cancel\n- **Right-click** a node for the context menu (add child, delete, etc.)\n- **Line number gutter** (left side) — shows sequential line numbers with selection highlight\n\n---\n\n### Drag-to-Reorder\n\n- **Drag** any node to reorder within its parent\n- Drop indicators show **before**, **after**, or **as child** insertion positions\n- Dragging between XML fragments is supported\n\n---\n\n### Search / Filter\n\nPress `Ctrl+F` or click the search button to open the filter bar.\n\n- Filters the tree in real-time as you type\n- Matches **tag names**, **attribute keys**, **attribute values**, and **leaf content**\n- Only matching nodes and their ancestors are shown\n- Press `Escape` or click the search button again to clear\n\n---\n\n### Options Menu\n\n- **Wrap Text** — toggle word wrap (affects horizontal scroll behaviour)\n- **Show Line Numbers** — show or hide the line-number gutter\n\n---\n\n### Keyboard Shortcuts\n\n- `Ctrl+F` — open/close search\n- `Tab` / `Enter` — commit in-place edit\n- `Escape` — cancel edit or close search\n\n---","screenshot":""},{"key":"UmlWindow","text":"## UmlWindow\n\nThe **UML Window** is an interactive UML class diagram editor supporting\nsix relationship types, auto-layout, and SAI/Gorp XML import.\n\n---\n\n### Layout Overview\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  [Auto-layout]  [Import]  [Save]            [?] [−] [×]         │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                                  │\n│    ┌───────────────┐          ┌─────────────────┐               │\n│    │  ClassName    │ ──────▷  │  AnotherClass   │               │\n│    │───────────────│          │─────────────────│               │\n│    │ + field: Type │          │ + method(): void│               │\n│    │───────────────│          └─────────────────┘               │\n│    │ + method()    │                                             │\n│    └───────────────┘                                             │\n│                                                                  │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Class Boxes\n\nEach class box has three sections: **name**, **attributes**, and **methods**.\n\n- **Click** to select a class\n- **Drag** to move the class box on the canvas\n- **Double-click** the class name to rename it\n- **Right-click** for the context menu:\n  - Add attribute / Add method\n  - Delete class\n  - Connect From Here (start a relationship)\n\n---\n\n### Members (Attributes & Methods)\n\n- **Double-click** a member to rename it in-place\n- **Drag** members to reorder within the class or move to another class\n- **Right-click** a member for options (delete, change visibility)\n- Visibility icons: `+` public, `-` private, `#` protected, `~` package\n\n---\n\n### Relationships\n\nSix relationship types are supported:\n\n| Symbol | Type | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| ──────▷ | Association | General use/reference |\n| ───────▷ | Dependency | Temporary dependency |\n| ──────▻ | Realization | Implements interface |\n| ──────▷ | Inheritance | Extends class |\n| ◇──────  | Aggregation | Has-a (weak) |\n| ◆──────  | Composition | Has-a (strong, owned) |\n\n- **Connect From Here** — right-click a class, choose *Connect From Here*, then click the target class\n- Hover over a relationship line to see its type label; after 2.5 s a tooltip shows the full description\n- Parallel connections between the same two classes are automatically separated by 25 px\n- Multiplicity labels appear along relationship lines (e.g. `1`, `0..*`)\n\n---\n\n### Canvas\n\n- **Left-drag** empty canvas to pan\n- **Right-click** canvas for: Add Class, Auto-Layout, Import, Save\n- **Auto-Layout** — arranges all classes automatically to avoid overlaps\n\n---\n\n### File Operations\n\n- **Save** — serialises the diagram to XML and saves to GitHub\n- **Import** — loads from a SAI XML, Gorp XML, or custom UML XML file\n- Files are loaded from GitHub or StreamingAssets fallback on open\n\n---","screenshot":""},{"key":"XmlWindow","text":"## XmlWindow\n\nThe **XML Window** is a hierarchical XML tree editor with in-place editing,\ndrag-to-reorder, search filtering, and GitHub sync.\n\n---\n\n### Layout Overview\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  [Search ⌕]  [</> Validate]  [⚙ Options]     [?] [−] [×]       │\n├──┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  │ ▼ root                                                        │\n│  │   ▼ element  attr=\"value\"                                     │\n│Line│       leaf content                                          │\n│Nos│   ▶ collapsed                                                │\n│   │                                                              │\n└──┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Title Bar Buttons\n\n- **⌕** — Toggle the search/filter bar (`Ctrl+F` / `Cmd+F`)\n- **</>** — Run XML well-formedness validation\n- **⚙** — Options menu (text wrapping, line numbers)\n\n---\n\n### Tree View\n\n- **▶ / ▼** — expand or collapse a node\n- **Click** a node to select it\n- **Double-click** a tag name, attribute value, or leaf content to edit it in-place\n  - `Tab` or `Enter` to commit\n  - `Escape` to cancel\n- **Right-click** a node for the context menu (add child, delete, etc.)\n- **Line number gutter** (left side) — shows sequential line numbers with selection highlight\n\n---\n\n### Drag-to-Reorder\n\n- **Drag** any node to reorder within its parent\n- Drop indicators show **before**, **after**, or **as child** insertion positions\n- Dragging between XML fragments is supported\n\n---\n\n### Search / Filter\n\nPress `Ctrl+F` or click the search button to open the filter bar.\n\n- Filters the tree in real-time as you type\n- Matches **tag names**, **attribute keys**, **attribute values**, and **leaf content**\n- Only matching nodes and their ancestors are shown\n- Press `Escape` or click the search button again to clear\n\n---\n\n### Options Menu\n\n- **Wrap Text** — toggle word wrap (affects horizontal scroll behaviour)\n- **Show Line Numbers** — show or hide the line-number gutter\n\n---\n\n### Keyboard Shortcuts\n\n- `Ctrl+F` — open/close search\n- `Tab` / `Enter` — commit in-place edit\n- `Escape` — cancel edit or close search\n\n---","screenshot":""},{"key":"ImageWindow","text":"## ImageWindow\n\nThe **Image Viewer** displays images dropped onto it and lets you save or\nexport them in PNG or JPG format.\n\n---\n\n### Layout Overview\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  [PNG / JPG]   image-name.png               [?] [−] [×]         │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                                  │\n│                   ┌────────────────┐                             │\n│                   │                │                             │\n│                   │    Image       │   (scale-to-fit)            │\n│                   │                │                             │\n│                   └────────────────┘                             │\n│                                                                  │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Opening Images\n\nDrop an image file onto the NOS desktop or dock.  Supported formats:\n**PNG**, **JPG / JPEG**, **GIF** (first frame), **BMP**, **TGA**.\n\n---\n\n### Format Toggle\n\nClick the **PNG / JPG** button in the title bar to switch the save format.\n\n- The file extension in the title bar updates to reflect the chosen format\n- On save or export, the image is re-encoded in the chosen format\n\n---\n\n### Save & Export\n\n- **Right-click the title bar** → **Save to GitHub** — saves the image to your GitHub-backed file storage\n- **Right-click the title bar** → **Export (Download)** — downloads the file to your browser's download folder\n\n---","screenshot":""},{"key":"PerformanceWindow","text":"## PerformanceWindow\n\nThe **Performance Monitor** shows real-time FPS and memory usage with\ncolour-coded threshold bars.  Toggle it with `Ctrl+M` (`Cmd+M` on Mac).\n\n---\n\n### Layout Overview\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  Performance                                 [?] [−] [×]        │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  FPS                    120 ████████████████░░░░  60 fps        │\n│  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────          │\n│  Managed Heap           512 MB ██████░░░░░░░░░  128 MB          │\n│  Total Allocated        512 MB ████░░░░░░░░░░░   98 MB          │\n│  Total Reserved         512 MB █████░░░░░░░░░░  110 MB          │\n│  Texture Memory         512 MB ██░░░░░░░░░░░░░   42 MB          │\n│  GFX Unused             512 MB █░░░░░░░░░░░░░░   18 MB          │\n│  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────          │\n│  Platform: WebGL  ·  Unity 6                                     │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Metrics\n\n#### FPS\n\nUpdates every 500 ms from a 60-sample rolling average.\n\n| Colour | Threshold |\n|---|---|\n| Green | > 45 FPS |\n| Yellow | 20 – 45 FPS |\n| Red | < 20 FPS |\n\n#### Memory\n\nMemory bars scale against a 512 MB cap. Bar colour:\n\n| Colour | Percentage of cap |\n|---|---|\n| Blue | < 50 % |\n| Yellow | 50 – 80 % |\n| Red | > 80 % |\n\nThe five memory categories are:\n\n- **Managed Heap** — C# garbage-collected heap (`GC.GetTotalMemory`)\n- **Total Allocated** — all Unity allocations\n- **Total Reserved** — pre-reserved Unity memory\n- **Texture Memory** — GPU texture memory\n- **GFX Unused Reserved** — reserved GPU memory not currently in use\n\nBar width transitions animate smoothly over 0.45 s.\n\n---\n\n### Keyboard Shortcut\n\n- `Ctrl+M` / `Cmd+M` — toggle the Performance Monitor from anywhere in NOS\n\n---","screenshot":""},{"key":"InputControlsWindow","text":"","screenshot":""},{"key":"XamlWindow","text":"## XamlWindow\n\nThe **XAML Window** is a full WPF XAML visual designer. It lets you build\nUI layouts by dragging controls onto a canvas, editing properties, writing\nsource code, and previewing live data bindings.\n\n---\n\n### Layout Overview\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  ≡  </>  ▶ Preview      [Title]               [?] [−] [×]      │  ← Title Bar\n├──────────┬──────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────┤\n│          │                              │  Properties            │\n│ Hierarchy│        Canvas               │  ─────────────────     │\n│  Tree    │   (visual XAML preview)     │  Data Context          │\n│          │                             │  ─────────────────     │\n│          ├─────────────────────────────┤                        │\n│          │  Source Code Panel          │                        │\n└──────────┴─────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────┘\n Palette strip (auto-hides on left edge)\n```\n\nAll panels are resizable by dragging the dividers between them.\n\n---\n\n### Title Bar Buttons\n\n- **≡** — Toggle the Hierarchy panel (left side tree view)\n- **</>** — Toggle the Source Code panel (bottom)\n- **▶ Preview** — Enter live data-binding preview mode (see Data Context below)\n- **◼ Preview** — Exit preview mode (shown when active)\n- **⊟** — Toggle the right panel (Properties + Data Context)\n\n---\n\n### Hierarchy Panel\n\nDisplays the XAML element tree on the left side.\n\n- Click any row to **select** that element on the canvas\n- **▶ / ▼** — expand or collapse a node's children\n- **·** — leaf node with no children\n- Row labels show the element type in teal, then `x:Name`, `Content`, or text hint in grey\n- **Drag rows** to reorder elements within their parent\n- Selection in the hierarchy auto-scrolls the source panel to the matching line\n- **≡** button in the title bar shows/hides this panel\n\n---\n\n### Canvas\n\nThe main visual editing area.\n\n- **Click** an element to select it (shows an 8-handle selection frame)\n- **Drag** the selected element to move it (updates `Canvas.Left` / `Canvas.Top`)\n- **Drag a resize handle** to resize (8 directions: corners + edges)\n- **Click empty space** to deselect\n- **Ctrl+C** — copy selected element\n- **Ctrl+X** — cut selected element\n- **Ctrl+V** — paste copied element\n- **Ctrl+D** — duplicate selected element\n- **Delete / Backspace** — delete selected element\n- **Shift+scroll** — horizontal pan\n- **2-finger trackpad** — horizontal and vertical pan\n\n---\n\n### Palette (auto-hide strip, left edge)\n\nMove the mouse to the far left edge to reveal the control palette.\n\nControls are grouped into six categories:\n\n| Group | Example Controls |\n|---|---|\n| Layout | Grid, StackPanel, Canvas, WrapPanel, DockPanel |\n| Controls | Button, TextBlock, TextBox, CheckBox, ComboBox |\n| Data | ListBox, ListView, DataGrid, TreeView |\n| Shapes | Rectangle, Ellipse, Path, Line, Polygon |\n| Media | Image, MediaElement, Viewbox |\n| Menus | Menu, ContextMenu, ToolBar, StatusBar |\n\n- **Drag** a tile from the palette onto the canvas or hierarchy to insert it\n- New elements receive sensible default attributes (size, position, content)\n- Dropping onto a container element inserts as a child\n\n---\n\n### Source Code Panel\n\nSyntax-highlighted XAML source at the bottom of the canvas area.\n\n- **Click a source row** to select the corresponding element in the hierarchy\n- Source scrolls to the selected element when you click in the hierarchy or canvas\n- **Drag source rows** to reorder elements (ghost label shows drag state)\n- Colour coding:\n  - **Teal** — element names\n  - **Cyan** — attribute names\n  - **Orange** — attribute values\n  - **Yellow** — `x:` prefixed attributes\n  - **Green** — comments\n\n---\n\n### Properties Panel\n\nShows all attributes of the selected element.\n\n- **Text fields** — edit attribute values directly; press Enter or click away to apply\n- **Colour swatches** — click to open the colour picker popup (24-colour grid + hex input)\n- **Binding pills** — cyan `{ }` pills indicate data-binding expressions; click **✏** to edit in the binding editor\n- **+ Add Attribute** button — adds a new attribute row to the selected element\n- **× buttons** — delete an attribute from the element\n- Changes apply live to the canvas and source panel simultaneously\n\n---\n\n### Binding Editor\n\nOpens when you click the **✏** button on a binding pill, or type a `{Binding ...}` expression into a property field and press Enter.\n\n#### Binding Kinds\n\n- **Binding** — resolves a path from the data context  \n  Fields: `Path`, `Mode`, `StringFormat`, `FallbackValue`, `TargetNullValue`, `Converter`\n- **StaticResource** — looks up a XAML resource by key  \n  Field: `Key` (with autocomplete from resources defined in the file)\n- **x:Static** — references a static member  \n  Fields: `Member` (format: `ns:Class.Property`)\n- **TemplateBinding** — binds to a template parent property\n- **RelativeSource** — binds relative to the element tree  \n  Fields: `Mode` (Self / FindAncestor / PreviousData), `AncestorType`\n- **Other** — freeform binding expression (raw text)\n\nClick **OK** to apply, or **Clear** to remove the binding and return to a plain value.\n\n---\n\n### Data Context Panel\n\nLocated below the Properties panel in the right column.\n\nLets you define a JSON data context and NCalc computed expressions so that\n`{Binding Path}` expressions can be resolved during **Preview mode**.\n\n#### JSON Tab\n\nPaste a JSON object representing your ViewModel:\n\n```\n{\n  \"Title\": \"Hello World\",\n  \"Count\": 42,\n  \"User\": { \"Name\": \"Alice\", \"Age\": 30 }\n}\n```\n\nClick **Apply** to parse the JSON. A green **● JSON valid** status confirms success.\nDotted paths like `User.Name` are automatically resolved.\n\n#### Computed Variables\n\nAdd computed expressions using NCalc syntax (`[VarName]` references JSON keys):\n\n| Name | Expression | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Full | `[First] + \" \" + [Last]` | Jane Doe |\n| Total | `[Price] * [Qty]` | 29.97 |\n\n- Click **+ Add** to add a row\n- Click **×** on a row to remove it\n- Expression errors show `[Error: Name]` in preview\n\n#### Preview Mode\n\nClick **▶ Preview** in the title bar to activate.\n\n- All `{Binding Path}` expressions on the canvas resolve to their data values\n- `{Binding Missing, FallbackValue=N/A}` shows `N/A` when a key is absent\n- `{Binding Count, StringFormat=Items: {0}}` shows `Items: 42`\n- StaticResource / TemplateBinding / RelativeSource are not resolved (kept as-is)\n- Click **◼ Preview** again to return to design mode\n\n---\n\n### Persistence\n\nAll panel states are automatically saved and restored:\n\n- Canvas scroll position and panel widths\n- Hierarchy expansion state\n- Selected node\n- JSON data context, computed expressions, and preview mode state\n\n---","screenshot":""},{"key":"XamlWindow","text":"## XamlWindow\n\nThe **XAML Window** is a full WPF XAML visual designer. It lets you build\nUI layouts by dragging controls onto a canvas, editing properties, writing\nsource code, and previewing live data bindings.\n\n---\n\n### Layout Overview\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  ≡  </>  ▶ Preview      [Title]               [?] [−] [×]      │  ← Title Bar\n├──────────┬──────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────┤\n│          │                              │  Properties            │\n│ Hierarchy│        Canvas               │  ─────────────────     │\n│  Tree    │   (visual XAML preview)     │  Data Context          │\n│          │                             │  ─────────────────     │\n│          ├─────────────────────────────┤                        │\n│          │  Source Code Panel          │                        │\n└──────────┴─────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────┘\n Palette strip (auto-hides on left edge)\n```\n\nAll panels are resizable by dragging the dividers between them.\n\n---\n\n### Title Bar Buttons\n\n- **≡** — Toggle the Hierarchy panel (left side tree view)\n- **</>** — Toggle the Source Code panel (bottom)\n- **▶ Preview** — Enter live data-binding preview mode (see Data Context below)\n- **◼ Preview** — Exit preview mode (shown when active)\n- **⊟** — Toggle the right panel (Properties + Data Context)\n\n---\n\n### Hierarchy Panel\n\nDisplays the XAML element tree on the left side.\n\n- Click any row to **select** that element on the canvas\n- **▶ / ▼** — expand or collapse a node's children\n- **·** — leaf node with no children\n- Row labels show the element type in teal, then `x:Name`, `Content`, or text hint in grey\n- **Drag rows** to reorder elements within their parent\n- Selection in the hierarchy auto-scrolls the source panel to the matching line\n- **≡** button in the title bar shows/hides this panel\n\n---\n\n### Canvas\n\nThe main visual editing area.\n\n- **Click** an element to select it (shows an 8-handle selection frame)\n- **Drag** the selected element to move it (updates `Canvas.Left` / `Canvas.Top`)\n- **Drag a resize handle** to resize (8 directions: corners + edges)\n- **Click empty space** to deselect\n- **Ctrl+C** — copy selected element\n- **Ctrl+X** — cut selected element\n- **Ctrl+V** — paste copied element\n- **Ctrl+D** — duplicate selected element\n- **Delete / Backspace** — delete selected element\n- **Shift+scroll** — horizontal pan\n- **2-finger trackpad** — horizontal and vertical pan\n\n---\n\n### Palette (auto-hide strip, left edge)\n\nMove the mouse to the far left edge to reveal the control palette.\n\nControls are grouped into six categories:\n\n| Group | Example Controls |\n|---|---|\n| Layout | Grid, StackPanel, Canvas, WrapPanel, DockPanel |\n| Controls | Button, TextBlock, TextBox, CheckBox, ComboBox |\n| Data | ListBox, ListView, DataGrid, TreeView |\n| Shapes | Rectangle, Ellipse, Path, Line, Polygon |\n| Media | Image, MediaElement, Viewbox |\n| Menus | Menu, ContextMenu, ToolBar, StatusBar |\n\n- **Drag** a tile from the palette onto the canvas or hierarchy to insert it\n- New elements receive sensible default attributes (size, position, content)\n- Dropping onto a container element inserts as a child\n\n---\n\n### Source Code Panel\n\nSyntax-highlighted XAML source at the bottom of the canvas area.\n\n- **Click a source row** to select the corresponding element in the hierarchy\n- Source scrolls to the selected element when you click in the hierarchy or canvas\n- **Drag source rows** to reorder elements (ghost label shows drag state)\n- Colour coding:\n  - **Teal** — element names\n  - **Cyan** — attribute names\n  - **Orange** — attribute values\n  - **Yellow** — `x:` prefixed attributes\n  - **Green** — comments\n\n---\n\n### Properties Panel\n\nShows all attributes of the selected element.\n\n- **Text fields** — edit attribute values directly; press Enter or click away to apply\n- **Colour swatches** — click to open the colour picker popup (24-colour grid + hex input)\n- **Binding pills** — cyan `{ }` pills indicate data-binding expressions; click **✏** to edit in the binding editor\n- **+ Add Attribute** button — adds a new attribute row to the selected element\n- **× buttons** — delete an attribute from the element\n- Changes apply live to the canvas and source panel simultaneously\n\n---\n\n### Binding Editor\n\nOpens when you click the **✏** button on a binding pill, or type a `{Binding ...}` expression into a property field and press Enter.\n\n#### Binding Kinds\n\n- **Binding** — resolves a path from the data context  \n  Fields: `Path`, `Mode`, `StringFormat`, `FallbackValue`, `TargetNullValue`, `Converter`\n- **StaticResource** — looks up a XAML resource by key  \n  Field: `Key` (with autocomplete from resources defined in the file)\n- **x:Static** — references a static member  \n  Fields: `Member` (format: `ns:Class.Property`)\n- **TemplateBinding** — binds to a template parent property\n- **RelativeSource** — binds relative to the element tree  \n  Fields: `Mode` (Self / FindAncestor / PreviousData), `AncestorType`\n- **Other** — freeform binding expression (raw text)\n\nClick **OK** to apply, or **Clear** to remove the binding and return to a plain value.\n\n---\n\n### Data Context Panel\n\nLocated below the Properties panel in the right column.\n\nLets you define a JSON data context and NCalc computed expressions so that\n`{Binding Path}` expressions can be resolved during **Preview mode**.\n\n#### JSON Tab\n\nPaste a JSON object representing your ViewModel:\n\n```\n{\n  \"Title\": \"Hello World\",\n  \"Count\": 42,\n  \"User\": { \"Name\": \"Alice\", \"Age\": 30 }\n}\n```\n\nClick **Apply** to parse the JSON. A green **● JSON valid** status confirms success.\nDotted paths like `User.Name` are automatically resolved.\n\n#### Computed Variables\n\nAdd computed expressions using NCalc syntax (`[VarName]` references JSON keys):\n\n| Name | Expression | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Full | `[First] + \" \" + [Last]` | Jane Doe |\n| Total | `[Price] * [Qty]` | 29.97 |\n\n- Click **+ Add** to add a row\n- Click **×** on a row to remove it\n- Expression errors show `[Error: Name]` in preview\n\n#### Preview Mode\n\nClick **▶ Preview** in the title bar to activate.\n\n- All `{Binding Path}` expressions on the canvas resolve to their data values\n- `{Binding Missing, FallbackValue=N/A}` shows `N/A` when a key is absent\n- `{Binding Count, StringFormat=Items: {0}}` shows `Items: 42`\n- StaticResource / TemplateBinding / RelativeSource are not resolved (kept as-is)\n- Click **◼ Preview** again to return to design mode\n\n---\n\n### Persistence\n\nAll panel states are automatically saved and restored:\n\n- Canvas scroll position and panel widths\n- Hierarchy expansion state\n- Selected node\n- JSON data context, computed expressions, and preview mode state\n\n---","screenshot":""},{"key":"XamlWindow","text":"## XamlWindow\n\nThe **XAML Window** is a full WPF XAML visual designer. It lets you build\nUI layouts by dragging controls onto a canvas, editing properties, writing\nsource code, and previewing live data bindings.\n\n---\n\n### Layout Overview\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  ≡  </>  ▶ Preview      [Title]               [?] [−] [×]      │  ← Title Bar\n├──────────┬──────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────┤\n│          │                              │  Properties            │\n│ Hierarchy│        Canvas               │  ─────────────────     │\n│  Tree    │   (visual XAML preview)     │  Data Context          │\n│          │                             │  ─────────────────     │\n│          ├─────────────────────────────┤                        │\n│          │  Source Code Panel          │                        │\n└──────────┴─────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────┘\n Palette strip (auto-hides on left edge)\n```\n\nAll panels are resizable by dragging the dividers between them.\n\n---\n\n### Title Bar Buttons\n\n- **≡** — Toggle the Hierarchy panel (left side tree view)\n- **</>** — Toggle the Source Code panel (bottom)\n- **▶ Preview** — Enter live data-binding preview mode (see Data Context below)\n- **◼ Preview** — Exit preview mode (shown when active)\n- **⊟** — Toggle the right panel (Properties + Data Context)\n\n---\n\n### Hierarchy Panel\n\nDisplays the XAML element tree on the left side.\n\n- Click any row to **select** that element on the canvas\n- **▶ / ▼** — expand or collapse a node's children\n- **·** — leaf node with no children\n- Row labels show the element type in teal, then `x:Name`, `Content`, or text hint in grey\n- **Drag rows** to reorder elements within their parent\n- Selection in the hierarchy auto-scrolls the source panel to the matching line\n- **≡** button in the title bar shows/hides this panel\n\n---\n\n### Canvas\n\nThe main visual editing area.\n\n- **Click** an element to select it (shows an 8-handle selection frame)\n- **Drag** the selected element to move it (updates `Canvas.Left` / `Canvas.Top`)\n- **Drag a resize handle** to resize (8 directions: corners + edges)\n- **Click empty space** to deselect\n- **Ctrl+C** — copy selected element\n- **Ctrl+X** — cut selected element\n- **Ctrl+V** — paste copied element\n- **Ctrl+D** — duplicate selected element\n- **Delete / Backspace** — delete selected element\n- **Shift+scroll** — horizontal pan\n- **2-finger trackpad** — horizontal and vertical pan\n\n---\n\n### Palette (auto-hide strip, left edge)\n\nMove the mouse to the far left edge to reveal the control palette.\n\nControls are grouped into six categories:\n\n| Group | Example Controls |\n|---|---|\n| Layout | Grid, StackPanel, Canvas, WrapPanel, DockPanel |\n| Controls | Button, TextBlock, TextBox, CheckBox, ComboBox |\n| Data | ListBox, ListView, DataGrid, TreeView |\n| Shapes | Rectangle, Ellipse, Path, Line, Polygon |\n| Media | Image, MediaElement, Viewbox |\n| Menus | Menu, ContextMenu, ToolBar, StatusBar |\n\n- **Drag** a tile from the palette onto the canvas or hierarchy to insert it\n- New elements receive sensible default attributes (size, position, content)\n- Dropping onto a container element inserts as a child\n\n---\n\n### Source Code Panel\n\nSyntax-highlighted XAML source at the bottom of the canvas area.\n\n- **Click a source row** to select the corresponding element in the hierarchy\n- Source scrolls to the selected element when you click in the hierarchy or canvas\n- **Drag source rows** to reorder elements (ghost label shows drag state)\n- Colour coding:\n  - **Teal** — element names\n  - **Cyan** — attribute names\n  - **Orange** — attribute values\n  - **Yellow** — `x:` prefixed attributes\n  - **Green** — comments\n\n---\n\n### Properties Panel\n\nShows all attributes of the selected element.\n\n- **Text fields** — edit attribute values directly; press Enter or click away to apply\n- **Colour swatches** — click to open the colour picker popup (24-colour grid + hex input)\n- **Binding pills** — cyan `{ }` pills indicate data-binding expressions; click **✏** to edit in the binding editor\n- **+ Add Attribute** button — adds a new attribute row to the selected element\n- **× buttons** — delete an attribute from the element\n- Changes apply live to the canvas and source panel simultaneously\n\n---\n\n### Binding Editor\n\nOpens when you click the **✏** button on a binding pill, or type a `{Binding ...}` expression into a property field and press Enter.\n\n#### Binding Kinds\n\n- **Binding** — resolves a path from the data context  \n  Fields: `Path`, `Mode`, `StringFormat`, `FallbackValue`, `TargetNullValue`, `Converter`\n- **StaticResource** — looks up a XAML resource by key  \n  Field: `Key` (with autocomplete from resources defined in the file)\n- **x:Static** — references a static member  \n  Fields: `Member` (format: `ns:Class.Property`)\n- **TemplateBinding** — binds to a template parent property\n- **RelativeSource** — binds relative to the element tree  \n  Fields: `Mode` (Self / FindAncestor / PreviousData), `AncestorType`\n- **Other** — freeform binding expression (raw text)\n\nClick **OK** to apply, or **Clear** to remove the binding and return to a plain value.\n\n---\n\n### Data Context Panel\n\nLocated below the Properties panel in the right column.\n\nLets you define a JSON data context and NCalc computed expressions so that\n`{Binding Path}` expressions can be resolved during **Preview mode**.\n\n#### JSON Tab\n\nPaste a JSON object representing your ViewModel:\n\n```\n{\n  \"Title\": \"Hello World\",\n  \"Count\": 42,\n  \"User\": { \"Name\": \"Alice\", \"Age\": 30 }\n}\n```\n\nClick **Apply** to parse the JSON. A green **● JSON valid** status confirms success.\nDotted paths like `User.Name` are automatically resolved.\n\n#### Computed Variables\n\nAdd computed expressions using NCalc syntax (`[VarName]` references JSON keys):\n\n| Name | Expression | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Full | `[First] + \" \" + [Last]` | Jane Doe |\n| Total | `[Price] * [Qty]` | 29.97 |\n\n- Click **+ Add** to add a row\n- Click **×** on a row to remove it\n- Expression errors show `[Error: Name]` in preview\n\n#### Preview Mode\n\nClick **▶ Preview** in the title bar to activate.\n\n- All `{Binding Path}` expressions on the canvas resolve to their data values\n- `{Binding Missing, FallbackValue=N/A}` shows `N/A` when a key is absent\n- `{Binding Count, StringFormat=Items: {0}}` shows `Items: 42`\n- StaticResource / TemplateBinding / RelativeSource are not resolved (kept as-is)\n- Click **◼ Preview** again to return to design mode\n\n---\n\n### Persistence\n\nAll panel states are automatically saved and restored:\n\n- Canvas scroll position and panel widths\n- Hierarchy expansion state\n- Selected node\n- JSON data context, computed expressions, and preview mode state\n\n---","screenshot":""},{"key":"XamlWindow","text":"## XamlWindow\n\nThe **XAML Window** is a full WPF XAML visual designer. It lets you build\nUI layouts by dragging controls onto a canvas, editing properties, writing\nsource code, and previewing live data bindings.\n\n---\n\n### Layout Overview\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  ≡  </>  ▶ Preview      [Title]               [?] [−] [×]      │  ← Title Bar\n├──────────┬──────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────┤\n│          │                              │  Properties            │\n│ Hierarchy│        Canvas               │  ─────────────────     │\n│  Tree    │   (visual XAML preview)     │  Data Context          │\n│          │                             │  ─────────────────     │\n│          ├─────────────────────────────┤                        │\n│          │  Source Code Panel          │                        │\n└──────────┴─────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────┘\n Palette strip (auto-hides on left edge)\n```\n\nAll panels are resizable by dragging the dividers between them.\n\n---\n\n### Title Bar Buttons\n\n- **≡** — Toggle the Hierarchy panel (left side tree view)\n- **</>** — Toggle the Source Code panel (bottom)\n- **▶ Preview** — Enter live data-binding preview mode (see Data Context below)\n- **◼ Preview** — Exit preview mode (shown when active)\n- **⊟** — Toggle the right panel (Properties + Data Context)\n\n---\n\n### Hierarchy Panel\n\nDisplays the XAML element tree on the left side.\n\n- Click any row to **select** that element on the canvas\n- **▶ / ▼** — expand or collapse a node's children\n- **·** — leaf node with no children\n- Row labels show the element type in teal, then `x:Name`, `Content`, or text hint in grey\n- **Drag rows** to reorder elements within their parent\n- Selection in the hierarchy auto-scrolls the source panel to the matching line\n- **≡** button in the title bar shows/hides this panel\n\n---\n\n### Canvas\n\nThe main visual editing area.\n\n- **Click** an element to select it (shows an 8-handle selection frame)\n- **Drag** the selected element to move it (updates `Canvas.Left` / `Canvas.Top`)\n- **Drag a resize handle** to resize (8 directions: corners + edges)\n- **Click empty space** to deselect\n- **Ctrl+C** — copy selected element\n- **Ctrl+X** — cut selected element\n- **Ctrl+V** — paste copied element\n- **Ctrl+D** — duplicate selected element\n- **Delete / Backspace** — delete selected element\n- **Shift+scroll** — horizontal pan\n- **2-finger trackpad** — horizontal and vertical pan\n\n---\n\n### Palette (auto-hide strip, left edge)\n\nMove the mouse to the far left edge to reveal the control palette.\n\nControls are grouped into six categories:\n\n| Group | Example Controls |\n|---|---|\n| Layout | Grid, StackPanel, Canvas, WrapPanel, DockPanel |\n| Controls | Button, TextBlock, TextBox, CheckBox, ComboBox |\n| Data | ListBox, ListView, DataGrid, TreeView |\n| Shapes | Rectangle, Ellipse, Path, Line, Polygon |\n| Media | Image, MediaElement, Viewbox |\n| Menus | Menu, ContextMenu, ToolBar, StatusBar |\n\n- **Drag** a tile from the palette onto the canvas or hierarchy to insert it\n- New elements receive sensible default attributes (size, position, content)\n- Dropping onto a container element inserts as a child\n\n---\n\n### Source Code Panel\n\nSyntax-highlighted XAML source at the bottom of the canvas area.\n\n- **Click a source row** to select the corresponding element in the hierarchy\n- Source scrolls to the selected element when you click in the hierarchy or canvas\n- **Drag source rows** to reorder elements (ghost label shows drag state)\n- Colour coding:\n  - **Teal** — element names\n  - **Cyan** — attribute names\n  - **Orange** — attribute values\n  - **Yellow** — `x:` prefixed attributes\n  - **Green** — comments\n\n---\n\n### Properties Panel\n\nShows all attributes of the selected element.\n\n- **Text fields** — edit attribute values directly; press Enter or click away to apply\n- **Colour swatches** — click to open the colour picker popup (24-colour grid + hex input)\n- **Binding pills** — cyan `{ }` pills indicate data-binding expressions; click **✏** to edit in the binding editor\n- **+ Add Attribute** button — adds a new attribute row to the selected element\n- **× buttons** — delete an attribute from the element\n- Changes apply live to the canvas and source panel simultaneously\n\n---\n\n### Binding Editor\n\nOpens when you click the **✏** button on a binding pill, or type a `{Binding ...}` expression into a property field and press Enter.\n\n#### Binding Kinds\n\n- **Binding** — resolves a path from the data context  \n  Fields: `Path`, `Mode`, `StringFormat`, `FallbackValue`, `TargetNullValue`, `Converter`\n- **StaticResource** — looks up a XAML resource by key  \n  Field: `Key` (with autocomplete from resources defined in the file)\n- **x:Static** — references a static member  \n  Fields: `Member` (format: `ns:Class.Property`)\n- **TemplateBinding** — binds to a template parent property\n- **RelativeSource** — binds relative to the element tree  \n  Fields: `Mode` (Self / FindAncestor / PreviousData), `AncestorType`\n- **Other** — freeform binding expression (raw text)\n\nClick **OK** to apply, or **Clear** to remove the binding and return to a plain value.\n\n---\n\n### Data Context Panel\n\nLocated below the Properties panel in the right column.\n\nLets you define a JSON data context and NCalc computed expressions so that\n`{Binding Path}` expressions can be resolved during **Preview mode**.\n\n#### JSON Tab\n\nPaste a JSON object representing your ViewModel:\n\n```\n{\n  \"Title\": \"Hello World\",\n  \"Count\": 42,\n  \"User\": { \"Name\": \"Alice\", \"Age\": 30 }\n}\n```\n\nClick **Apply** to parse the JSON. A green **● JSON valid** status confirms success.\nDotted paths like `User.Name` are automatically resolved.\n\n#### Computed Variables\n\nAdd computed expressions using NCalc syntax (`[VarName]` references JSON keys):\n\n| Name | Expression | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Full | `[First] + \" \" + [Last]` | Jane Doe |\n| Total | `[Price] * [Qty]` | 29.97 |\n\n- Click **+ Add** to add a row\n- Click **×** on a row to remove it\n- Expression errors show `[Error: Name]` in preview\n\n#### Preview Mode\n\nClick **▶ Preview** in the title bar to activate.\n\n- All `{Binding Path}` expressions on the canvas resolve to their data values\n- `{Binding Missing, FallbackValue=N/A}` shows `N/A` when a key is absent\n- `{Binding Count, StringFormat=Items: {0}}` shows `Items: 42`\n- StaticResource / TemplateBinding / RelativeSource are not resolved (kept as-is)\n- Click **◼ Preview** again to return to design mode\n\n---\n\n### Persistence\n\nAll panel states are automatically saved and restored:\n\n- Canvas scroll position and panel widths\n- Hierarchy expansion state\n- Selected node\n- JSON data context, computed expressions, and preview mode state\n\n---","screenshot":""},{"key":"XamlWindow","text":"## XamlWindow\n\nThe **XAML Window** is a full WPF XAML visual designer. It lets you build\nUI layouts by dragging controls onto a canvas, editing properties, writing\nsource code, and previewing live data bindings.\n\n---\n\n### Layout Overview\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  ≡  </>  ▶ Preview      [Title]               [?] [−] [×]      │  ← Title Bar\n├──────────┬──────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────┤\n│          │                              │  Properties            │\n│ Hierarchy│        Canvas               │  ─────────────────     │\n│  Tree    │   (visual XAML preview)     │  Data Context          │\n│          │                             │  ─────────────────     │\n│          ├─────────────────────────────┤                        │\n│          │  Source Code Panel          │                        │\n└──────────┴─────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────┘\n Palette strip (auto-hides on left edge)\n```\n\nAll panels are resizable by dragging the dividers between them.\n\n---\n\n### Title Bar Buttons\n\n- **≡** — Toggle the Hierarchy panel (left side tree view)\n- **</>** — Toggle the Source Code panel (bottom)\n- **▶ Preview** — Enter live data-binding preview mode (see Data Context below)\n- **◼ Preview** — Exit preview mode (shown when active)\n- **⊟** — Toggle the right panel (Properties + Data Context)\n\n---\n\n### Hierarchy Panel\n\nDisplays the XAML element tree on the left side.\n\n- Click any row to **select** that element on the canvas\n- **▶ / ▼** — expand or collapse a node's children\n- **·** — leaf node with no children\n- Row labels show the element type in teal, then `x:Name`, `Content`, or text hint in grey\n- **Drag rows** to reorder elements within their parent\n- Selection in the hierarchy auto-scrolls the source panel to the matching line\n- **≡** button in the title bar shows/hides this panel\n\n---\n\n### Canvas\n\nThe main visual editing area.\n\n- **Click** an element to select it (shows an 8-handle selection frame)\n- **Drag** the selected element to move it (updates `Canvas.Left` / `Canvas.Top`)\n- **Drag a resize handle** to resize (8 directions: corners + edges)\n- **Click empty space** to deselect\n- **Ctrl+C** — copy selected element\n- **Ctrl+X** — cut selected element\n- **Ctrl+V** — paste copied element\n- **Ctrl+D** — duplicate selected element\n- **Delete / Backspace** — delete selected element\n- **Shift+scroll** — horizontal pan\n- **2-finger trackpad** — horizontal and vertical pan\n\n---\n\n### Palette (auto-hide strip, left edge)\n\nMove the mouse to the far left edge to reveal the control palette.\n\nControls are grouped into six categories:\n\n| Group | Example Controls |\n|---|---|\n| Layout | Grid, StackPanel, Canvas, WrapPanel, DockPanel |\n| Controls | Button, TextBlock, TextBox, CheckBox, ComboBox |\n| Data | ListBox, ListView, DataGrid, TreeView |\n| Shapes | Rectangle, Ellipse, Path, Line, Polygon |\n| Media | Image, MediaElement, Viewbox |\n| Menus | Menu, ContextMenu, ToolBar, StatusBar |\n\n- **Drag** a tile from the palette onto the canvas or hierarchy to insert it\n- New elements receive sensible default attributes (size, position, content)\n- Dropping onto a container element inserts as a child\n\n---\n\n### Source Code Panel\n\nSyntax-highlighted XAML source at the bottom of the canvas area.\n\n- **Click a source row** to select the corresponding element in the hierarchy\n- Source scrolls to the selected element when you click in the hierarchy or canvas\n- **Drag source rows** to reorder elements (ghost label shows drag state)\n- Colour coding:\n  - **Teal** — element names\n  - **Cyan** — attribute names\n  - **Orange** — attribute values\n  - **Yellow** — `x:` prefixed attributes\n  - **Green** — comments\n\n---\n\n### Properties Panel\n\nShows all attributes of the selected element.\n\n- **Text fields** — edit attribute values directly; press Enter or click away to apply\n- **Colour swatches** — click to open the colour picker popup (24-colour grid + hex input)\n- **Binding pills** — cyan `{ }` pills indicate data-binding expressions; click **✏** to edit in the binding editor\n- **+ Add Attribute** button — adds a new attribute row to the selected element\n- **× buttons** — delete an attribute from the element\n- Changes apply live to the canvas and source panel simultaneously\n\n---\n\n### Binding Editor\n\nOpens when you click the **✏** button on a binding pill, or type a `{Binding ...}` expression into a property field and press Enter.\n\n#### Binding Kinds\n\n- **Binding** — resolves a path from the data context  \n  Fields: `Path`, `Mode`, `StringFormat`, `FallbackValue`, `TargetNullValue`, `Converter`\n- **StaticResource** — looks up a XAML resource by key  \n  Field: `Key` (with autocomplete from resources defined in the file)\n- **x:Static** — references a static member  \n  Fields: `Member` (format: `ns:Class.Property`)\n- **TemplateBinding** — binds to a template parent property\n- **RelativeSource** — binds relative to the element tree  \n  Fields: `Mode` (Self / FindAncestor / PreviousData), `AncestorType`\n- **Other** — freeform binding expression (raw text)\n\nClick **OK** to apply, or **Clear** to remove the binding and return to a plain value.\n\n---\n\n### Data Context Panel\n\nLocated below the Properties panel in the right column.\n\nLets you define a JSON data context and NCalc computed expressions so that\n`{Binding Path}` expressions can be resolved during **Preview mode**.\n\n#### JSON Tab\n\nPaste a JSON object representing your ViewModel:\n\n```\n{\n  \"Title\": \"Hello World\",\n  \"Count\": 42,\n  \"User\": { \"Name\": \"Alice\", \"Age\": 30 }\n}\n```\n\nClick **Apply** to parse the JSON. A green **● JSON valid** status confirms success.\nDotted paths like `User.Name` are automatically resolved.\n\n#### Computed Variables\n\nAdd computed expressions using NCalc syntax (`[VarName]` references JSON keys):\n\n| Name | Expression | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Full | `[First] + \" \" + [Last]` | Jane Doe |\n| Total | `[Price] * [Qty]` | 29.97 |\n\n- Click **+ Add** to add a row\n- Click **×** on a row to remove it\n- Expression errors show `[Error: Name]` in preview\n\n#### Preview Mode\n\nClick **▶ Preview** in the title bar to activate.\n\n- All `{Binding Path}` expressions on the canvas resolve to their data values\n- `{Binding Missing, FallbackValue=N/A}` shows `N/A` when a key is absent\n- `{Binding Count, StringFormat=Items: {0}}` shows `Items: 42`\n- StaticResource / TemplateBinding / RelativeSource are not resolved (kept as-is)\n- Click **◼ Preview** again to return to design mode\n\n---\n\n### Persistence\n\nAll panel states are automatically saved and restored:\n\n- Canvas scroll position and panel widths\n- Hierarchy expansion state\n- Selected node\n- JSON data context, computed expressions, and preview mode state\n\n---","screenshot":""},{"key":"XamlGorpWindow","text":"","screenshot":""},{"key":"GorpEquationWindow","text":"## GorpEquationWindow\n\nThe **Gorp Equation Window** is a visual mathematical expression editor.\nBuild equations by combining nodes on an interactive canvas, then save the\nresult as a MathML-compatible Gorp algorithm.\n\n---\n\n### Layout Overview\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  Gorp Equation                               [?] [−] [×]        │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                                  │\n│    x  +  ( a  ×  b )                                            │\n│    ▲       ▲     ▲                                              │\n│  [slot]  [slot] [slot]                                           │\n│                                                                  │\n│  (right-click canvas for Undo / Redo)                           │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Building Expressions\n\n- **Click a slot** (grey placeholder) to open the slot editor\n- In the slot editor, choose a node type:\n  - **Variable** — a named input (e.g. `x`, `count`)\n  - **Literal** — a numeric constant (e.g. `42`, `3.14`)\n  - **Unary** — negation `–`, square root `√`, or parentheses `( )`\n  - **Binary** — `+`, `–`, `×`, `÷`, `^` (power)\n  - **Comparison** — `<`, `>`, `≤`, `≥`, `=`\n  - **Logical** — `AND`, `OR`, `NOT`\n- Each node that accepts operands shows sub-slots for its children\n\n---\n\n### Editing Nodes\n\n- **Click** a node to select it\n- **Right-click** a node for options:\n  - Delete node\n  - Wrap in negation / parentheses / square root\n  - For power nodes: *Delete Power, keep base* / *keep exponent* / *Delete Upwards chain*\n- **Double-click** a variable or literal to rename/change its value\n\n---\n\n### Undo / Redo\n\n- **Ctrl+Z** — undo last change\n- **Ctrl+Shift+Z** — redo\n- **Right-click the canvas background** — shows Undo / Redo options when available\n- History is kept up to **50 steps**\n\n---\n\n### Saving\n\nRight-click the title bar → **Save to GitHub** to persist the equation as\na Gorp algorithm XML file.","screenshot":""}]}